e is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=2,\\,{m}_{2}=2,\\,{m}_{3}=3,\\,{m}_{4}=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=3,\\,{y}_{2}=5,\\,{y}_{3}=2,\\,{y}_{4}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =2+2+3+1 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3}+{m}_{4}{y}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6+10+6+4 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{26}{8}=\\frac{13}{4}.\n$$" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309231 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309232 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309233 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309234 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309235 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1041 "selection" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309234 13194139534773 true] [17592186309230 1110 #uuid "0c4040e3-8350-548f-9e5f-98b284791773" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309231 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186