-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/ec39adee65bb0219053a8802470534cf8b2588f95cc8338c5c4a392adac6d516.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-m\\cdot 4=-4m\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $4\\cdot 6=24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24-4m & =0 \\\\ 4m & =24 \\\\ m & =6\\,kg.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309238 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309239 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309240 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309241 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309242 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1041 "selection" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309239 13194139534773 true] [17592186309237 1110 #uuid "6025c73a-0b67-58d7-9bab-4e3984a7af53" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309238 1034 "4\\,kg" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309238 1111 #uuid "be5b0627-bf7e-5a07-9053-c832cc2e5a99" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309239 1034 "6\\,kg" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309239 1111 #uuid "cefaf9ba-7d38-529c-bdbd-825c73bb2b09" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309240 1034 "6.5\\,kg" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309240 1111 #uuid "686a4c5a-e510-5952-81cb-4558f85b8be5" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309241 1034 "5\\,kg" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309241 1111 #uuid "a8d5a419-88c1-5fd6-b6e3-b1f9cac36ed5" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309242 1034 "4.5\\,kg" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309242 1111 #uuid "f91c6308-1e03-53d7-a410-0b45a2535726" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309243 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309244 13194139534773 true] [17592186309243 1089 "q-163803" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309243 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534773 true] [17592186309243 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/1292177200af79b36b05111607a33d0057d417c3e2f432de8439defb44e8928e.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $12\\,yd$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $A$ has mass $6\\,lb$ and is $4\\,yd$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $B.$" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309243 1113 #uuid "5c95ea01-feae-5636-bd7f-4cd1ac42fa53" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309243 1145 "Let $m$ be the mass of $B.$\nThe length of the rod is $12\\,yd$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is $4\\,yd.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is\n\n$$\n12-4=8\\,yd,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/97c638d214774f8517b2724aabf8c91a1cc6b543f1ae17c5ba632acbe1ec59ff.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-6\\cdot 4=-24\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $m\\cdot 8=8m\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-24+8m & =0 \\\\ 8m & =24 \\\\ m & =3\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309245 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309246 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309247 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309248 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309249 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1041 "selection" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309245 13194139534773 true] [17592186309244 1110 #uuid "4cbce05a-d0b3-54ec-9211-e55e4feaeb2e" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309245 1034 "3\\,lb" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309245 1111 #uuid "2e54b040-651f-5b72-9f63-fede4e7ca214" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309246 1034 "4.3\\,lb" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309246 1111 #uuid "9e3f6751-7ef9-52f4-83ac-210d2e0f1348" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309247 1034 "4\\,lb" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309247 1111 #uuid "86010cd5-581b-5a23-90c1-4ad63893a8d5" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309248 1034 "2.5\\,lb" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309248 1111 #uuid "c0eeda1f-5303-5f80-b066-34abebfdca42" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309249 1034 "3.8\\,lb" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534773 true] [17592186309249 1111 #uuid "191c9c5f-b811-51a3-9a12-069cc2759f03" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309250 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309251 13194139534773 true] [17592186309250 1089 "q-163831" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309250 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534773 true] [17592186309250 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/088d73d81b8b1705f8ff329ff38b8cd289bd8ecbe48ffc4c0bd18c823635b418.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $8\\,kg$ and $4\\,kg$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $6\\,m$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. Find the distance between the fulcrum and $B.$" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309250 1113 #uuid "1b5967cb-a959-5be0-9c19-f06b6c3ac38a" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309250 1145 "Let ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}$ be the distances between the fulcrum and $A$ and $B$, respectively, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/31dd97f05b7dde8459bf79efbebcac082571c49282aeb63f926b0c1c058923c8.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-8\\cdot {d}_{1}=-8{d}_{1}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $4\\cdot {d}_{2}=4{d}_{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe principle of moments tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n4{d}_{2}-8{d}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe need to find ${d}_{2},$ so we eliminate ${d}_{1}.$\nUsing the fact that the rod has length $6\\,m,$ we have\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}+{d}_{2}=6\\,⟹\\,{d}_{1}=6-{d}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{d}_{2}-8(6-{d}_{2}) & =0 \\\\ 4{d}_{2}-48+8{d}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 12{d}_{2} & =48 \\\\ {d}_{2} & =4\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534773 true] [17592186309251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309252 13194139534773 true] [17592186309251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309253 13194139534773 true] [17592186309251 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309254 1